VALUES (623, '1A', $t$ASK 623: Gemini 4 Hydrogen and Gemini 4 Neon debate and judge$t$,
  $t$The operator can choose Gemini 4 Neon or Gemini 4 Hydrogen as either debater, and can place each as a panel judge or an alternate on the Judge order page. Both seats stand under every rule that binds the present seats: no judge of a debater's family; no judge running a debater's model (ASK 601); the enforcer never of a debater's family (ASK 608); a panel of exactly three. LIVE on write (ruling 512). (plan rev 0, OBJECTIVE, ask623/w4/plan623.md 87989e36)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at 16:01 CST 2026-11-24 on the card "Write it" in W4's thread (Wall 11742; audit 41709). Database, in one transaction: a new model_config row neon (google/gemini-4-neon, family google, no reasoning field; the hydrogen row unchanged); neon added to the seat list of odv1_record_panel_substitution and to dash_judge_lineup, dash_odv1_debates and dash_odv1_judges; hydrogen and neon added to dash_debaters (the launch list, now 12 debaters); hydrogen and neon appended to the judge order as alternates 6 and 7 with a log row. Engine 0d55aab1 to 20db58ee-a005-4ecc-8313-258833c915a7, five nodes, seat tables only: Init Seats (the debater list gains hydrogen and neon; the family table and JFAM gain neon), Resolve Seats, Build Synthesis, Build Independent Verdict and Build Diagnostic Prompt (JFAM gains neon). Child and Library untouched; no prompt text changed; no reasoning or effort setting added; nothing deleted. W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11743). The engine manual entry was written by W3 at 16:27 CST on its own card (part 10.0 v310; Wall 11754; audit 41725; W1 readback MATCH, Wall 11755). Shown offline: 132 pairings, 128 seat three judges and 4 stop with the ASK 608 reason as before; on the 90 present pairings no judge, reserve or enforcer changes (68 change only in the tail of the alternates list); Neon against Hydrogen is judged by sol62, spark and sol with luna enforcing; the 8 new pairings of a Google debater against chatgpt or sol62 seat spark, qwen4max and sonnet with glm enforcing and have no reserve and no alternate, so 12 pairings now have none. Each model returned a complete debate answer in one paid check call with no reasoning setting (Hydrogen execution 42337, Neon execution 42339; 0.369 dollars together). Departures from what was pressed, both stated to the operator: the plan card's default "neither placed in the judge order until you save it" could not work, because the Judge order page cannot add a seat, so he pressed to append both; and the judge order reads version 5, not 3 as the write card said, because two rolled-back dry runs used log ids 3 and 4 (the order's contents are as pressed). As alternates the two seats can be offered a removed judge's seat with no Save, after the alternates ahead of them. Not shown by a run: neither seat has debated under its own name, the engine has never called neon in any role, and no run has been made since the write. Open: each seat in a live run in each role, two clean live runs per path (the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24). RUN REVISION (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42373-tg0w4edj (debate_results e7f6922f, row created 17:21 CST 2026-11-24; engine 20db58ee, child 74353c40; anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 as the Oracle defending against anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; outcome UNDERDETERMINED, panel BROKEN 2-1). The always line is shown: the judge order line reads version 5 and its alternates list ends hydrogen, neon; both seats were asked and accepted in the AGREEMENT block. UNEXERCISED: neither seat debated or judged. In this run no panel send-back was sent (53 of 58 rows read "NOT SENT: no panel request for this seat"; the cause is the ASK 611 build, since fixed by fix 2 and not shown by a run), so nothing that needs a panel send-back was shown. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'.$t$,
